#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Release authorisation and review follow draft-to-publication.bpmn. The site is published from the AST on the IG's cache branch (ig-ast-cache.bpmn). A release is started by the owner pushing a `v*` tag of the current version (`ig-release.bpmn`, which also holds the catch-up when a version was not tagged): the IG's `ig-release.yml` runs a full AST build, then `ig-release.ts` makes a GitHub DRAFT release carrying `package.tgz` (and its R4/R4B variants), `ast-data.zip` and `SHA256SUMS`; the owner publishing that draft is Task_AuthorizeRelease (skill `ig-binary-artefacts` §\"Releasing\"). The site serves each resource as a reduced `<Type>-<id>.json` at its root; the full copies are the release's and the AST cache's."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run the IG Publisher: it renders output/, writes each resource's JSON, the package, canonicals and qa.json, and does the two things no cache can — validates every resource against its profiles and resolves the dependency closure with terminology expansion."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Source model ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:35
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Task_AuthorFsh is the single re-entry point for both failure paths: an invalid-FHIR loop from Gateway_Valid, which leaves no record, and a QC failure, which arrives after Task_QcBeans has filed it. Which edge fired is the only signal that tells a mechanical re-run from a finding to read."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:126
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The IG draws on library sources; every statement extracted from them is published as pages of the IG and in the shared extraction viewer, each linked to its library entry and section, before the IG Publisher builds the site. The sub-process is core's, the same for every content type: this IG supplies only the page look (its pages' table class) and registers the pages in its own menu. The generated pages are checked for staleness in CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The IG's source model is ready: l3-fhir-authoring's required sourceModel. Which model, and how it was produced, is the calling process's to say; this pipeline names none."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The last lane, with no path back into the loop: reaching it means Task_IgPublisher succeeded on Lane_Qc's clean verdict. It does not itself decide whether the release is authorised: that call is draft-to-publication.bpmn's, and Task_PublishIg only executes what that separate process has already cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The QC reviewer rules on the aggregate QA against the publication gates. Emitting the QA report is mechanical; ruling on it is the reviewer's decision."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:51
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single gate between valid FHIR JSON and the full IG Publisher build: Task_IgPublisher runs only once this lane says clean, so a compiling-but-wrong profile never reaches a publishable IG."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two jobs share this lane. Task_Sushi and Task_Validate turn FSH into validated FHIR JSON and loop back to the modeller lane on failure with no bean filed: re-running compile-and-validate is cheap. Task_IgPublisher runs only once Lane_Qc has passed, and its output is what Lane_PubMgr publishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:85
#. Diagram label
msgid "Validate against profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Validate the compiled resources against their profiles and the packages they constrain. A validator that could not start is could-not-determine, never a pass with an empty findings list. Failures return to authoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:22
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan (beans)"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write the FSH profiles, value sets and definitions the source model calls for. This is the stage where profiles, slicing and invariants belong — a decision that can only be expressed in FHIR comes here, not back into the source model."
msgstr ""

